| Codes to tags: a style begin or end code becomes a tag named by the style; every other code becomes a processing code <?$ ... `>
| This should be run first, before italic treatment.
| 1;1 2011-2-14 P Sullivan, from txxsgm.sbt
| states: 1 = normal text
|   3 = inside general (or unrecognized) begin-tag
|   4 = inside general (or unrecognized) end-tag
|   5 = inside processing code
| Tags treated generally
| Begin tags
es=~<~~3~
es|~~<~~3~
.~>~3~1~
~>~3~1~
| End tags
ee=~</~~4~
ee|~~</~~4~
.~>~4~1~
~>~4~1~
| Processing codes
~<?$~~5~
~`>~5~1~
